            "exploitScenario": "An attacker arranges for the victim's return-to cookie to hold https://evil.example (e.g., via an app flow or subdomain that sets return-to). On the next request through the Edge middleware, proxy.ts:86 computes new URL('https://evil.example', <self-url>) which - per the user-provided nuance - follows the absolute value and ignores the base, producing a 307 redirect to evil.example. No same-origin check or getSafeRedirectUrl is applied (the cookie is only .delete()'d at proxy.ts:89), so the user is redirected off-origin (phishing / token leakage).",
            "confidence": "high",
